<article class="env-lemma" id="065V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065V">Lemma <span data-tag="065V">10.134.7</span>.</a> Let $A \to B \to C$ be ring maps. Assume $A \to C$ is surjective (so also $B \to C$ is). Denote $I = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A \to C)$ and $J = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(B \to C)$. Then the sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  I/I^2 \to J/J^2 \to \Omega _{B/A} \otimes _ B B/J \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> is exact. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/00S2" data-tag="00S2">10.134.4</a> and the description of the naive cotangent complexes $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/B}$ and $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{C/A}$ in Lemma <a href="/tag/07BP" data-tag="07BP">10.134.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>